       from the reference (active space, orbitals) rather than the perturbation theory.

  SLOPE of the triplet energy over 1.639-1.739 A (band width scales with it):
    SC  -5.977 eV/A    FIC -5.912 eV/A    FIC/SC = 0.989
    (vertical-energy slope: SC -6.335, FIC -6.330 eV/A)
    -> Same shape within 3%. The SC surface is fine for the band width;
       only its absolute position needs correcting (dCCSD(T) splice or a shift).

  COST per geometry, wall: orbitals 23 s, FIC 3 s (two states), SC 2 s (two states)
  For a raster only the triplet is needed per point, so roughly half of each NEVPT2 figure.
